---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/pages/the-work.css';
---

<Layout title="SP+: Secure Prospective" description="SP+ is an immutable, encrypted, contained, AI-first workstation for insurance agents and financial advisors.">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="work-page" transition:name="page-card">
    <section class="work-hero" aria-labelledby="work-title" data-deal>
      <div class="work-hero-inner shell">
        <div class="work-hero-copy">
          <h1 id="work-title">SP+.</h1>
          <div class="work-status-bar" aria-label="SP+ build status">
            <span>DELIVERABLE // 001</span>
            <span>STATE // IN BUILD</span>
          </div>
          <p class="work-manifest">Immutable. Encrypted.<br />Contained. AI-First.</p>
          <p class="work-hero-lede">
            A safer workstation for professionals trusted with other people’s financial lives.
          </p>
          <div class="work-hero-actions">
            <a class="action action--dark" href="#security">Read the foundation <span class="action-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
            <span class="work-honesty">BUILD STATUS / active work</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="system-plate" data-system-map aria-labelledby="system-map-title">
          <div class="plate-head">
            <span id="system-map-title">SYSTEM MAP // REPRESENTATION</span>
            <span>SP+ / 001</span>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-body">
            <div class="plate-route" aria-label="Representation of the SP+ workflow">
              <div class="plate-node plate-node--input">
                <span>INPUT</span>
                <strong>Advisor’s desk</strong>
                <small>Screenshot or plain-text question</small>
              </div>
              <span class="plate-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <div class="plate-node plate-node--core">
                <span>SP+ // CORE</span>
                <strong>Controlled workstation</strong>
                <small>Fedora-based immutable image</small>
              </div>
              <span class="plate-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <div class="plate-node plate-node--output">
                <span>OUTPUT</span>
                <strong>Plain-English steps</strong>
                <small>Human-held guidance</small>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="foundation-inspector">
              <span class="inspector-label">INSPECT THE FOUNDATION</span>
              <div class="foundation-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="SP+ foundation controls">
                <button id="tab-encrypted" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="foundation-panel" data-map-tab="encrypted">Encrypted</button>
                <button id="tab-immutable" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="foundation-panel" data-map-tab="immutable">Immutable</button>
                <button id="tab-contained" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="foundation-panel" data-map-tab="contained">Contained</button>
              </div>
              <div id="foundation-panel" class="foundation-panel" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="tab-encrypted" data-map-panel>
                <span data-map-panel-label>FOUNDATION // ENCRYPTED</span>
                <strong data-map-panel-title>Encrypted from installation</strong>
                <p data-map-panel-copy>Full-disk encryption is built into the setup model.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <figcaption>A representation of the operating model, not a screenshot. The product is in build.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="work-hero-foot shell" aria-label="SP+ status details">
        <span>FEDORA-BASED // IMMUTABLE IMAGE</span>
        <span>HUMAN-HELD // AI-ASSISTED</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="premise" class="work-section work-premise" aria-labelledby="premise-title" data-deal>
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="work-section-rail"><span>01</span><span>THE STARTING POINT</span></div>
        <div class="work-premise-grid">
          <h2 id="premise-title">General convenience is not a security model.</h2>
          <div class="work-copy">
            <p>
              Most independent advisors work on off-the-shelf computers running on residential Wi-Fi,
              exposed to intrusive pop-ups, background update risk, and un-sandboxed applications. The same
              workstation handles sensitive client PII, fixed annuities, and retirement assets on infrastructure
              built for casual home browsing.
            </p>
            <p>
              SP+ changes the starting point. It is a Fedora-based immutable desktop engineered for insurance
              agents and financial advisors who need a controlled, hardened environment without hiring an IT
              department or becoming system administrators themselves.
            </p>

            <div class="starting-line" aria-label="The change SP+ makes to the starting point">
              <div class="starting-line-field">
                <span>GENERAL STARTING POINT</span>
                <strong>Casual home browsing</strong>
              </div>
              <span class="starting-line-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <div class="starting-line-field starting-line-field--new">
                <span>SP+ STARTING POINT</span>
                <strong>Controlled, hardened environment</strong>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="security" class="work-section work-security" aria-labelledby="security-title" data-deal>
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="work-section-rail"><span>02</span><span>SECURITY // DEFENSIBLE PROTECTION</span></div>
        <div class="work-section-heading">
          <h2 id="security-title">Security by design.</h2>
          <p>Three controls make the foundation legible before the advisor has to rely on it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="security-manifest" aria-label="SP+ security foundations">
          <div class="security-manifest-label">
            <span>FOUNDATION</span>
            <strong>The first layer is the point.</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="security-list">
            <article class="security-row" data-foundation-row="encrypted">
              <span class="security-row-index">01</span>
              <div class="security-row-copy">
                <span>FOUNDATION // ENCRYPTED</span>
                <h3>Encrypted from installation</h3>
                <p>Full-disk encryption is built into the setup model, protecting client files when a laptop is lost, misplaced, or stolen.</p>
              </div>
              <span class="security-row-state">BUILT INTO SETUP</span>
            </article>
            <article class="security-row" data-foundation-row="immutable">
              <span class="security-row-index">02</span>
              <div class="security-row-copy">
                <span>FOUNDATION // IMMUTABLE</span>
                <h3>A controlled operating foundation</h3>
                <p>The core system is immutable and updated as a managed image, reducing accidental damage, configuration drift, and unauthorized background modification.</p>
              </div>
              <span class="security-row-state">MANAGED IMAGE</span>
            </article>
            <article class="security-row" data-foundation-row="contained">
              <span class="security-row-index">03</span>
              <div class="security-row-copy">
                <span>FOUNDATION // CONTAINED</span>
                <h3>Containment where it matters</h3>
                <p>Applications are isolated wherever practical. If one app is compromised, containment limits the blast radius and makes lateral movement harder.</p>
              </div>
              <span class="security-row-state">LIMITED BLAST RADIUS</span>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="reality-note">
          <div>
            <h3>Not a magic wand. A stronger foundation.</h3>
            <span>THE REALITY CHECK</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            SP+ is not a replacement for multi-factor authentication, secure email, offsite backups, or a
            formal compliance program. The goal is not perfect security. It is a smaller attack surface and a
            foundation you can inspect.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="workflow" class="work-section work-workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title" data-deal>
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="work-section-rail"><span>03</span><span>WORKFLOW // HUMAN-HELD</span></div>
        <div class="work-section-heading work-section-heading--split">
          <h2 id="workflow-title">Human-held, AI-assisted workflows.</h2>
          <p>
            Technology should not get in the way of writing business. SP+ integrates the Pi AI harness into
            the daily desktop environment and connects it to the advisor’s existing Claude or ChatGPT subscription.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="workflow-route" aria-labelledby="workflow-route-title">
          <figcaption id="workflow-route-title" class="sr-only">Advisor workflow through the Pi AI harness</figcaption>
          <div class="workflow-stage workflow-stage--input">
            <span>INPUT A</span>
            <strong>Visual screenshot</strong>
            <small>Show the bottleneck.</small>
          </div>
          <span class="workflow-route-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="workflow-stage workflow-stage--core">
            <span>CO-PILOT</span>
            <strong>Pi AI harness</strong>
            <small>Human-held, AI-assisted.</small>
          </div>
          <span class="workflow-route-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="workflow-stage workflow-stage--output">
            <span>OUTPUT</span>
            <strong>Plain-English steps</strong>
            <small>Know what to click next.</small>
          </div>
        </figure>

        <div class="workflow-support">
          <div>
            <span>GUIDANCE // VISUAL</span>
            <strong>Show the bottleneck</strong>
            <p>Snap a screenshot when migrating email, setting up DNS, or navigating a carrier portal.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span>GUIDANCE // DIRECT</span>
            <strong>Know what to click next</strong>
            <p>Receive step-by-step instructions in plain English and return focus to client cases.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="evidence" class="work-section work-evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title" data-deal>
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="work-section-rail"><span>04</span><span>EVIDENCE // BUILT FROM EXPERIENCE</span></div>
        <div class="work-section-heading work-section-heading--compact">
          <h2 id="evidence-title">Built from experience, not theory.</h2>
          <p>SP+ is being built by someone who has worked across the technical, physical, and financial consequences around the desk.</p>
        </div>

        <table class="experience-register" aria-label="Experience behind SP+">
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">26 years in technology</th>
              <td>Hands-on experience with operating-system architecture, system hardening, field deployment, and open-source reliability.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">15 years in electrical and low voltage</th>
              <td>A physical-infrastructure mindset: grounded systems built to remain reliable under consequence.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">6 years in insurance and annuities</th>
              <td>First-hand experience with compliance pressure, carrier portals, advisor workflows, and the reality of writing business.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">$110M+ annuity production assisted</th>
              <td>Designed by someone who understands the financial value of the business sitting on the advisor’s desk.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="method" class="work-section work-method" aria-labelledby="method-title" data-deal>
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="work-section-rail"><span>05</span><span>METHOD // APPLIED</span></div>
        <div class="work-section-heading work-section-heading--compact">
          <h2 id="method-title">Diagnose. Position. Shape. Transform.</h2>
          <p>SP+ applies the same discipline to the workstation that it applies to every operating constraint.</p>
        </div>

        <ol class="method-track">
          <li>
            <span class="method-track-index">01</span>
            <strong>Diagnose</strong>
            <p>Start with the real advisor workstation, its risks, interruptions, and obligations.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="method-track-index">02</span>
            <strong>Position</strong>
            <p>Place security controls and AI assistance where they improve the work without taking ownership away.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="method-track-index">03</span>
            <strong>Shape</strong>
            <p>Turn technical friction into plain-language guidance the advisor can understand and act on.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="method-track-index">04</span>
            <strong>Transform</strong>
            <p>Replace the casual home-computer starting point with an operating foundation built for the practice.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="access" class="work-section work-access" aria-labelledby="access-title" data-deal>
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="work-section-rail"><span>06</span><span>ACCESS // PARTNERSHIP MODEL</span></div>
        <div class="work-section-heading work-section-heading--compact">
          <h2 id="access-title">SP+ costs nothing but the opportunity to work with us.</h2>
          <p>
            There is no software fee and no recurring SP+ subscription invoice. Access is earned through a
            five-production-contract partnership selected with Christopher Campbell. The partnership comes
            first. The workstation follows.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="access-status" aria-label="SP+ access terms">
          <div><span>SOFTWARE FEE</span><strong>None</strong></div>
          <div><span>RECURRING SP+ INVOICE</span><strong>None</strong></div>
          <div><span>QUALIFICATION</span><strong>5 production contracts</strong></div>
        </div>

        <ol class="access-path">
          <li>
            <span>01</span>
            <div><strong>Fit review</strong><p>Start with the practice, existing producer relationships, current workstation, and intended use. Christopher determines whether an operating fit exists.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>02</span>
            <div><strong>Five-contract qualification</strong><p>Establish five production contracts selected with Christopher. Those contracts are the business relationship exchanged for SP+ access.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>03</span>
            <div><strong>Compatibility confirmation</strong><p>Confirm the computer, installation path, migration scope, and support expectations. SP+ is not represented as compatible with every machine.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>04</span>
            <div><strong>SP+ deployment</strong><p>Receive the encrypted immutable OS image and Pi harness integration, connected to an existing Claude or ChatGPT subscription.</p></div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="access-terms">
          <section>
            <h3>Access includes</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Fedora-based immutable OS image</li>
              <li>Full-disk encryption setup model</li>
              <li>Practical application containment</li>
              <li>Pi AI harness integration</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section>
            <h3>Access does not replace</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Multi-factor authentication</li>
              <li>Secure email and offsite backups</li>
              <li>A formal compliance program</li>
              <li>A separate Claude or ChatGPT subscription</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section>
            <h3>Confirmed before setup</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Selected production contracts</li>
              <li>Hardware compatibility</li>
              <li>Installation and migration scope</li>
              <li>Support expectations</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>

        <div class="access-close">
          <p>Start with the practice. Confirm the fit. Let the workstation follow the relationship.</p>
          <a class="action action--signal" href="mailto:secureprospective@gmail.com?subject=SP%2B%20fit%20review">Start an SP+ fit review <span class="action-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../scripts/motion.js';
  import '../scripts/pages/the-work.js';
</script>
